module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoherentNoetherian
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoherentSubquotient
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasicoherentCartesianOnAffineCharts
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.QuasicoherentFromCoherence

/-!
# Submodules and quotient modules of a coherent module on a locally Noetherian algebraic space

Let `F` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` which is locally Noetherian and let `M` be a
coherent `𝒪_F`-module.  Stacks 07UD asserts that a quasi-coherent submodule of `M` and a
quasi-coherent quotient module of `M` are again coherent.  **Both assertions are proved here.**

Both are false without local Noetherianity: over the spectrum of a valuation ring of rank one
which is not discrete the structure sheaf is coherent, finitely generated ideals being
principal, while its maximal ideal is a quasi-coherent submodule which is not of finite type and
the residue field is a quasi-coherent quotient module which is not coherent.  What local
Noetherianity buys is the single assertion that a quasi-coherent submodule of a coherent module
is of finite type, and that assertion is the content of this file; the passage from it to the two
assertions of Stacks 07UD is `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoherentSubquotient`, which
needs no Noetherianity.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiniteType_of_mono_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`: **a quasi-coherent
  submodule of a coherent module on a locally Noetherian algebraic space is of finite type.**
  This is the one place where local Noetherianity enters.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCoherentOnSite_of_mono_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCoherent_of_mono_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`: **the submodule
  assertion of Stacks 07UD.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCoherentOnSite_of_epi_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCoherent_of_epi_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`: **the quotient assertion
  of Stacks 07UD.**

## Implementation notes

The argument is local on an étale chart `V` which is affine with Noetherian ring of sections
`A = 𝒪_F(V)` and over which `M` is generated by finitely many sections `s₁, …, sₙ`.  Such charts
cover the small étale site: the charts carrying finitely many generators of `M` cover it because
`M` is of finite type, generation is inherited by restriction, and every chart is covered by
affine charts with Noetherian rings of sections, which is what local Noetherianity gives through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_covering_through_noetherianAffine`.

Over such a `V` the submodule `N ⊆ M` is generated by finitely many sections, obtained as
follows.  The coefficient tuples `x ∈ Aⁿ` with `∑ xᵢ sᵢ` a section of `N` form a submodule of
`Aⁿ`, namely the relations among the images of the `sᵢ` in `M(V)/N(V)`, so they are generated by
finitely many tuples `g₁, …, g_k` because `Aⁿ` is a Noetherian module — no finiteness of `M(V)`
is used, exactly as in `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_generators_relations_of_isCartesian`.  The
sections `tⱼ ∈ N(V)` with `ι(tⱼ) = ∑ᵢ gⱼᵢ sᵢ` are the generators.  That they generate is the base
change step: a section of `N` over a chart is, locally, an `𝒪_F`-combination of the `sᵢ` because
the `sᵢ` generate `M`, and the coefficient tuple of such a combination is an `𝒪_F`-combination of
the `gⱼ` because flat base change carries the generating tuples over `V` onto the generating
tuples over any affine chart over `V`.

That base change step is where Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) is used, in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`: it is applied to
`M`, which is quasi-coherent because it is coherent on the site, and to `N`, which is
quasi-coherent by hypothesis, and it turns both into the statement that their sections over an
affine chart over `V` are the base change of their sections over `V`.  Nothing is carried as a
hypothesis: the two cartesian properties are discharged, and the only inputs beyond the source's
own are the locally Noetherian `Fact` instance and quasi-coherence of the submodule.

For the quotient assertion the submodule in play is the kernel of the projection, which is
quasi-coherent by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_kernel` together with
Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) in both directions: the kernel of a morphism of modules cartesian on
affine charts is cartesian on affine charts, hence quasi-coherent.

The module universe is the universe `u` of the schemes, as it is in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoherentSubquotient`: that is the universe in which the
category of `𝒪_F`-modules is abelian and the universe at which Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) is
available.

The sums over the sections of a module are written with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrictLinear` rather than with
`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ`, because only the former has the ambient
`𝒪_F(V)`-module structure of the sections visible to instance search; the two are the same
function.

